        "steps": [
          "Open the supplied image with Pillow; package does not apply EXIF transpose. For controlled diagnostics, orient/crop externally before this recipe and record that choice.",
          "Convert to Pillow L mode (8-bit grayscale).",
          "Apply Pillow ImageOps.autocontrast with defaults (cutoff=0, ignore=None, preserve_tone=False). This is min/max contrast stretching, not histogram equalization; a constant image stays unchanged.",
          "Set scale=640/max(original_width, original_height); scaled_width=int(original_width*scale), scaled_height=int(original_height*scale), using truncation.",
          "Resize grayscale image to those integer dimensions using Pillow bilinear interpolation.",
          "Create a 640x640 L image filled with 0. Paste resized image at pad_x=(640-scaled_width)//2, pad_y=(640-scaled_height)//2; any odd extra pad falls at right/bottom.",
